{"id": "sdqa0007", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3097460736, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "What's the difference between man-slaughter and homicide?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0007.wav", "input_sha256": "b5dc29ee8e124e827cfdaf5e731d518c51f4ff1928c7f96aa9100fdf5acb4cf2", "input_samples": 101370, "input_s": 6.336, "n_real_chunks": 7, "score": 0.2929, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Homicide is the broad term for one person causing the death of another person. It can be lawful or unlawful—for example, murder, manslaughter, negligent homicide, or a justified killing in self-defense may all be considered homicides. Laws and terminology vary by jurisdiction.", "expert_answer": "**Homicide** is the broad term for one person causing the death of another person. It can be **lawful** or **unlawful**—for example, murder, manslaughter, negligent homicide, or a justified killing in self-defense may all be considered homicides.\n\n**Manslaughter** is a specific type of **unlawful homicide** that is generally less culpable than murder because it usually lacks “malice aforethought” or premeditated intent to kill.\n\nCommon categories:\n\n- **Voluntary manslaughter:** an intentional killing under mitigating circumstances, such as a sudden heat-of-passion killing after adequate provocation.\n- **Involuntary manslaughter:** an unintentional killing caused by reckless or criminally negligent conduct.\n\nSo, **all manslaughter is homicide, but not all homicide is manslaughter**. Laws and terminology vary by jurisdiction.", "transcript": "What's the difference between manslaughter and homicide?\n", "asr_s": 1.83, "expert_s": 4.07, "expert_input_samples": 101370, "expert_input_s": 6.336, "expert_input_sha256": "b5dc29ee8e124e827cfdaf5e731d518c51f4ff1928c7f96aa9100fdf5acb4cf2", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.105, "relay_synth_ms": 10803, "onset_chunk": 6, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0007_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "7d7088e30edd6d023fd57b1b01630beacd624ff021acca64fa955cf4c34a0549", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 20.36}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0007_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "511619beb5dbc8ce974cc310ee91afe3237deab259b2bb872ea2cb17c472fcf2", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0007_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "11d752953cc1ac74a28da0e8408fc0e1fc5ae4c54456c547947445394625da3b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.066, 1.124, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.072, 2.125, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.07, 3.127, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.08, 4.145, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.073, 5.138, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.073, 6.13, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 6.336, 6.413, 6.984, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 6.336, "last_real_feed_done": 6.413, "onset": 6.984, "gate_read_done": 6.984, "fire": 6.984, "candidate_first_pcm": 6.984, "stall_note": 6.986, "stall_first_pcm": 7.772, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 7.772, "expert_req": 6.986, "expert_resp": 12.877, "relay_synth_start": 12.878, "relay_first_pcm": 13.662, "relay_synth_end": 23.681, "first_any_pcm": 6.984, "first_answer_pcm": 13.662, "session_end": 23.853}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.327, "ttfa_any_s": 0.649}
{"id": "sdqa0017", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2709827905, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "When did Marxism develop?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0017.wav", "input_sha256": "c6b745ef8328a05cf2ad5dd1456d1566ee56271b5c3781987c40baf8cf67cebe", "input_samples": 55973, "input_s": 3.498, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.1533, "act": 0.9971, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Marxism developed in the mid-19th century, primarily in the 1840s, through the writings of Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels. A key early statement of Marxist ideas was The Communist Manifesto, published in 1848.", "expert_answer": "**Marxism developed in the mid-19th century**, primarily in the **1840s**, through the writings of **Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels**. A key early statement of Marxist ideas was **_The Communist Manifesto_**, published in **1848**.", "transcript": "When did Marxism develop?\n", "asr_s": 0.53, "expert_s": 1.93, "expert_input_samples": 55973, "expert_input_s": 3.498, "expert_input_sha256": "c6b745ef8328a05cf2ad5dd1456d1566ee56271b5c3781987c40baf8cf67cebe", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.855, "relay_synth_ms": 8038, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0017_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "c8c53ecf6d0d58462d8efa0520e560f04a1b9ac5a79b7e81331f52797bda9eac", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 14.72}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0017_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "20c3d98d4d04d441788f68c5d7c5d0adc2f47cb4e943ebd3ba10d07bdf2b61fb", "sr": 24000, "seconds